In article <10416@saturn.ADS.COM> xanthian@saturn.ADS.COM (Metafont Consultant Account) writes:

>>And someone has to do the dirty job -- draw all those monsters.

>the monsters/features can be drawn bigger and with more detail.

Even the "mighty blitter of Amiga" doesn't know what a leprechaun or
acid blob or blue jelly look like. Neither do I! The difficulty is to be
able to draw those monster so that we can tell which is which. And that
does mean, we need a bloody good artist! No computer phreaks to draw those
monsters..

Besides, if we add support for N+1 (N great) computers and graphics cards
and still let anyone make additions to the game, the source will become
unreadable and difficult to keep bug-free. Just look at all those patches
(7 of them) for 3.0.

Nethack is a piece of code that seriously would need object oriented 
programming! I realize that it won't be possible to convert it to another
language (because of its size), but something has to be done to organize it.
WHAT IS NEEDED MOST OF ALL is a guide to nethack programmers about nethack
source code, its c-files, header-files, data structures, etc. What I have
heard from the development team, no-one is familiar with the whole code..
This isn't critisism. I know they have done a great job, and I'm greateful,
but is DOES SHOW that such a document is needed. In fact, I believe that
just the creation of such a document will reveal basic faults and weaknesses
in the code. Remember, no amount of testing can be better than properly
designed code!
